    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d527">

                <pb facs="0974" n="960" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg960"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.CC/9–2244</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Myron C. Taylor, Personal Representative of
                        President Roosevelt to Pope Pius XII, to the President</hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d527-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vatican City</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-09-10">September 10, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. President</hi>: I recently wired you<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d527-f2"/> that His Holiness had requested more detailed
                    information than I had as yet seen fit to give to him in respect to the
                    International Organization for the Preservation of Peace.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d527-f3"/> In my wire I enquire to what extent Secretary Hull and
                    yourself wished me to go in explaining the details of the plan which I followed
                    in the consultations<anchor n="4" xml:id="d527-f4"/> which I had with Chief
                    Justice Hughes,<anchor n="5" xml:id="d527-f5"/> Honorable John W. Davis<anchor
                        n="6" xml:id="d527-f6"/> and Honorable Nathan L. Miller.<anchor n="7"
                        xml:id="d527-f7"/>
                </p>
                <p>I now have a similar written request from His Holiness, of which I am attaching a
                    copy. Your advice in the premises will be very greatly appreciated and with best
                    regards, believe me.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Myron</hi> C. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Taylor</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d527-a1.xml" xpointer="d527-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d527-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d527-f1-content">
                <p>Copy transmitted to the Secretary of State with the following memorandum of
                    September 22, 1944, from President Roosevelt: “For preparation of reply for my
                    signature.”</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d527-f2" n="2" xml:id="d527-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram 301, September 6, 10 a.m., not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d527-f3" n="3" xml:id="d527-f3-content">
                <p>For correspondence on this subject, see <ref target="#pg614">pp. 614</ref>
                    ff.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d527-f4" n="4" xml:id="d527-f4-content">
                <p>In April and May of 1944 Secretary of State Hull authorized Mr. Taylor, who was a
                    member of the Department of State Informal Political Agenda Group concerned with
                    a “Possible Plan for the Establishment of an International Organization for the
                    Maintenance of International Peace and Security”, to hold consultations with the
                    three jurists mentioned. See <hi rendition="#italic">Postwar Foreign Policy
                        Preparation, 1939–1945</hi> (Washington, Government Printing Office, 1949),
                    pp. 169–173, 247–255 and 263–265.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d527-f5" n="5" xml:id="d527-f5-content">
                <p>Charles Evans Hughes, Chief Justice of the United States, 1930–1941.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d527-f6" n="6" xml:id="d527-f6-content">
                <p>Democratic presidential candidate in 1924.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d527-f7" n="7" xml:id="d527-f7-content">
                <p>Governor of New York, 1921–1923.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
